From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:58:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 445/488] [DS4.1] Prefill SP attention front gathered without
 torch copies

The norms write the Q and KV halves into the all-gather's buffer in
place, a TileLang copy puts the index head weights beside them, and one
TileLang launch splits the gathered rows into contiguous parts: torch's
cat and three contiguous copies gone.
